 "notes": "Bordag-Mohideen-Mostepanenko Casimir review (Sec. 7, Fig. 28): constraints on the Yukawa correction V=-(GM1M2/r)(1+alpha_G exp(-r/lambda)) from Casimir force measurements. Curve traced from the vector EPS figCnew.eps in the arXiv e-print (fig2dev polylines, axes calibrated from tick labels). Reported curve is the envelope of the Casimir-derived constraints: curve 6 (AFM Casimir measurement with gold surfaces, Eqs. 7.16/7.22, strongest for 4.3e-9 m < lambda < 1.5e-7 m), curve 2 (Casimir measurements between dielectrics, Eq. 7.6, best in the gap), and curve 4a (Lamoreaux torsion-pendulum experiment, Eq. 7.15, alpha_G>0 branch chosen over the nearly identical alpha_G<0 curve 4b), spanning lambda = 4.0e-9 to 2.0e-4 m. Cavendish-type curve 1 and van der Waals curve 3 excluded (not Casimir-based). x-axis converted from range lambda to boson mass via m = 1.97e-7 eV*m / lambda. Native |alpha_G| reported; to convert to scalar-nucleon coupling in L = g phi NbarN use alpha = g^2 M_Pl^2/(4 pi m_N^2), i.e. g = sqrt(4 pi alpha) m_N/M_Pl (~2.7e-19 sqrt(alpha)). Paper quotes no explicit confidence level (constraints from |F_hyp| < absolute experimental error Delta F); 0.95 entered as nominal. Not a dark-matter search; no rho_DM assumed.",
